// Format: reset_dataA[3:0]_dataB[3:0]_ctrlA_ldA_ctrlB_ldB_Psel_ldP_Pexp[7:0]_b0exp_zexp
// Total: 24 bits per line

// Vector 1: Asynchronous System Reset. Expect outputs cleared, z=1 (since B=0)
0_0000_0000_0_0_0_0_0_0_00000000_0_1

// Vector 2: Load dataA=0100 (4) and dataB=1010 (10). Do not latch P yet.
// B is 1010, so its LSB b0=0, and z=0 (not zero).
1_0100_1010_1_1_1_1_0_0_00000000_0_0

// Vector 3: Shift Cycle! Left shift A (00000100 -> 00001000 = 8).
// Right shift B (1010 -> 0101 = 5). b0 becomes 1 (LSB of 0101). z remains 0.
1_0000_0000_0_1_0_1_0_0_00000000_1_0

// Vector 4: Latch raw 'A' into reg8. Psel=0, ldP=1.
// A is 8 (00001000). B stays 5 (0101). b0=1, z=0.
1_0000_0000_0_0_0_0_0_1_00001000_1_0

// Vector 5: Addition Mode! Latch A + B into reg8. Psel=1, ldP=1.
// A(8) + B(5) = 13 (00001101). b0=1, z=0.
1_0000_0000_0_0_0_0_1_1_00001101_1_0

// Vector 6: Clear shift register B to test the zero reduction flag 'z'.
// rst=1, ldB=1, ctrlB=1, dataB=0000. B becomes 0, so z rolls high (1), b0=0.
1_0000_0000_0_0_1_1_0_0_00001101_0_1